5 < 1 # The fleet: launcher, VM and record
6 < 1 
7 < 1 `fleet/CONTRACT.md` is the authority for every literal and `fleet/RUNBOOK.md` the operator
8 < 1 procedure; the contract wins. `fleet/` is laptop tools plus the VM bootstrap — the engine is
10 > 1 `factory/`, which imports no fleet file. No orchestrator, no
9 < 2 `factory/`, and the only fleet file it imports is `kata-client.mjs`. No orchestrator, no
10 < 1 control VM, no token on any VM or in any argv.
11 < 1 
12 < 1 ## A launch (`launch.mjs`, split by phase in #1307)
13 < 1 
14 < 1 1. Validate: the plan's hash pins (`plan-pins.mjs`), then `plan_check.py --base` through
15 < 1    `compiler.mjs`, which fetches and runs `plan_check.py` and `plan_parse.py` at `engine=`.
16 < 1    Its `STALE fact:`, `GREEN-AT-BASE fact:` and `AUTHORING fact:` lines print on the launch line. The VM is sized from
17 < 1    `plan_parse.py`'s widest wave. `toolchain.mjs` checks what a fresh sandbox can run.
18 < 1 2. Read the evidence repository (`--evidence-repo`, else `"evidence"` in
19 < 1    `~/.ultrapowers/fleet.json`; neither is a refusal) and the pool from `billing plan --json`;
20 < 1    compute N from the evidence repository's `live/<owner>-<repo>/run-*` branches and
21 < 1    `<owner>-<repo>/run-*` tags; refresh the Claude bearer (`claude-token.mjs`).
22 < 1 3. Push the plan as one parentless commit in the evidence repository (tree =
25 > 1    `runs/<owner>-<repo>/<N>/plan.md` and its siblings) to `live/<owner>-<repo>/run-<N>`. Nothing
26 < 1    else is told of the run: there is no issue board (the kata hub left on 2026-11-13).
24 > 2    `runs/<owner>-<repo>/<N>/plan.md` and its siblings) to `live/<owner>-<repo>/run-<N>`. The kata hub is
25 < 2    not asked: `launch.kata.mode` in `fleet/policy.json` is `off`, so there is no ping, nothing is
26 < 2    filed and the commit carries no `kata.json`, without which the sandbox writes nothing to Kata.
27 < 2    The rollback `on` pings the hub (a dark hub refuses the launch) and files the run there
28 < 2    (`kata-file.mjs`).
23 < 2    `runs/<owner>-<repo>/<N>/plan.md` and its siblings) to `live/<owner>-<repo>/run-<N>`; file the
24 < 2    run on the kata hub (`kata-file.mjs`).
25 < 1 4. Issue ONE lobby verb (`lobby.mjs`): `new` with VM name `fleet-r<N>-<stamp>-<rand>`,
26 < 1    `--tag fleet`, the assignment as `--comment`, both integrations, `--cpu`/`--memory` from
27 < 1    `~/.ultrapowers/fleet.json`, and the setup script (`setup-script.mjs`) on stdin. No image,
28 < 1    no attach, no ssh wait, no explicit start.
29 < 1 
30 < 1 On the VM the setup script writes the evidence repository to `$HOME/fleet-evidence-repo`
31 < 1 (the boot fails without it), installs the toolchain, the immutable bootstrap at
32 < 1 `/usr/local/lib/fleet/bootstrap.sh` and the `fleet-run@.service` template, then starts
33 < 1 `fleet-run@<N>.service`. The bootstrap reads the comment once, clones the engine at `engine=`
34 < 1 into `/home/exedev/engines/<sha>`, and execs its `factory/boot.sh` or refuses. It never
35 < 1 overwrites itself (run-68).
36 < 1 
37 < 1 ## The record
38 < 1 
39 < 1 The record lives in the operator's evidence repository, never on the target. The sandbox
41 > 1 commits it to `live/<owner>-<repo>/run-<N>` under `runs/<owner>-<repo>/<N>/` every 10 s and at
40 < 2 commits it to `live/<owner>-<repo>/run-<N>` under `runs/<owner>-<repo>/<N>/` every 60 s and at
41 < 1 each transition, pushes `ultra/integration-run-<N>` to the target (the only branch the target
42 < 1 receives; main's memory, `refs/ultrapowers/weave/v1`, is the one other ref, pushed by the publish
43 < 1 before every merge request) and opens its own PR over REST (`prAuthor` recorded). The PR is the gate. At the end of
44 < 1 every run (done, parked, failed) it tags the last commit `<owner>-<repo>/run-<N>`, verifies it
45 < 1 with `git ls-remote --tags`, then deletes the live branch; a tag that doesn't verify keeps it.
46 < 1 Read a past run at
47 < 1 `repos/<evidence repo>/contents/runs/<owner>-<repo>/<N>/status.json?ref=<owner>-<repo>/run-<N>`.
48 < 1 
